# Keep `sqlfluff lint` (run anywhere in the repo) focused on OUR SQL. Skip:
#  - the installed dbt packages: they ship their own deprecated .sqlfluff
#    configs (the tab_space_size / max_line_length / indent_unit warnings) and
#    integration-test models that aren't part of this dbt project ("... was not
#    found in dbt project"), and they're vendored, not ours to lint;
#  - dbt's build artifacts (compiled SQL, run logs);
#  - the Python venv, which vendors dbt-core's own global_project macros
#    (site-packages/dbt/include/...) — thousands of .sql files, not ours.
# The per-edit hooks and the pre-commit gate lint explicit file paths under
# transform/models|tests|macros, so none of this affects them.
venv/
transform/dbt_packages/
transform/target/
transform/logs/
